message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Mechanized Analysis of Post-Quantum Key-Update Proposals for CCSDS SDLS-EP"
abstract: >-
  Symbolic (Dolev-Yao) verification, in the Tamarin prover, of two proposed
  post-quantum extensions to the CCSDS Space Data Link Security Extended
  Procedures: the Triple-KEM/Dual-KEM key-update mechanism (Hulsing, Lange &
  Weber, CANS 2025) and E2EQSS (Wildfeuer et al., ESA 3S 2025). Triple-KEM is
  checked both as published (Fig. 1) and with a spacecraft-to-ground key
  confirmation added: as published, secrecy and the spacecraft's authentication
  of ground hold but ground's authentication of the spacecraft does not; with
  the confirmation, all properties verify. Makes Dual-KEM's security boundary
  precise, and reports FB-01: a rekey desynchronization under space channel
  constraints, with no defined recovery, that requires no cryptographic
  compromise and holds on both versions; a four-message fix is verified on
  both, including the condition (the spacecraft keeps the previous key) under
  which it is safe. Also shows E2EQSS is hybrid for confidentiality but not for
  authentication.
